WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.968 --> 00:00:01.734
-Nice to see you.
I wanted

00:00:01.734 --> 00:00:02.501
to start off the interview

00:00:02.501 --> 00:00:03.534
by showing a photo of you.

00:00:03.534 --> 00:00:05.000
-Uh-oh.
-This is posted

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.200
[ Laughter ]
by Dwyane Wade.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:08.634
-Oh, Lord.

00:00:08.634 --> 00:00:11.100
-Posted a picture of you.
-Oh, my goodness.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:18.334
-This is a young
Stephen A. Smith. College?

00:00:18.334 --> 00:00:19.734
-College at Winston-Salem State.

00:00:19.734 --> 00:00:21.267
But you see, this is bad, man,

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:24.300
because this dude, Dwyane Wade,

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.200
the dude that walks around
with pink pants on

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:29.367
[ Laughter ]
and the whole stuff.

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:32.300
He's got me because he's
a three-time champion,

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:34.167
a future first-ballot
Hall of Famer.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:37.200
So, when he says
he would drop 50 on me,

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.334
it's not like he's lying.

00:00:38.334 --> 00:00:39.234
[ Laughter ]
You know what?

00:00:39.234 --> 00:00:40.534
I'd be better than anybody

00:00:40.534 --> 00:00:42.033
I've seen on the Knicks lately.

00:00:42.033 --> 00:00:43.334
[ Laughter and oohs ]

00:00:43.334 --> 00:00:47.267
You know? I mean,
let me tell you something, man.

00:00:47.267 --> 00:00:49.067
I'm here today

00:00:49.067 --> 00:00:50.968
because "The Tonight Show."

00:00:50.968 --> 00:00:53.467
Jimmy Fallon called me
and it's my honor and privilege

00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:54.934
[ Faux-tearfully ]
to be here, but,

00:00:54.934 --> 00:00:56.434
[ Laughter ]
I'm getting emotional right now.

00:00:56.434 --> 00:00:57.567
-It's alright, bud.

00:00:57.567 --> 00:00:59.167
I know.

00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:01.467
-These dudes, man, these --
Hold.

00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:02.467
[ Laughter ]
[ Tender music plays ]

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:04.167
These dudes, man...
-The Knicks.

00:01:04.167 --> 00:01:05.667
-...they keep doing this to me.

00:01:05.667 --> 00:01:06.767
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:09.868
The other night,
they were up 17 points.

00:01:09.868 --> 00:01:10.868
[ Laughter ]
-I know, I know.

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:13.234
And I was on TV,
on "NBA Countdown,"

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:14.567
and I said, "You know what?

00:01:14.567 --> 00:01:15.834
It doesn't make any difference.

00:01:15.834 --> 00:01:16.901
They're never going to change.

00:01:16.901 --> 00:01:18.601
They're just going
to lose the lead."

00:01:18.601 --> 00:01:20.067
[ Laughter ]
And, sure enough, they did it.

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:21.901
[ Laughter ]
Sure enough, they did it.

00:01:21.901 --> 00:01:25.067
I mean, I'm asking you
to make me out to be a liar

00:01:25.067 --> 00:01:26.133
and you couldn't do that right.

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:26.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:26.834 --> 00:01:27.968
[ Sad trombone plays ]

00:01:27.968 --> 00:01:29.200
-I do want to discuss

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.367
more sports scenes with you,

00:01:30.367 --> 00:01:31.634
but first, there's something

00:01:31.634 --> 00:01:33.534
that I just loved about you.

00:01:33.534 --> 00:01:35.367
-Okay.
-I'm a fan, but,

00:01:35.367 --> 00:01:37.667
you are a character
on "General Hospital."

00:01:37.667 --> 00:01:40.300
[ Laughter ]
-Yes. Yeah.
-And I did not know this

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.300
but I am a giant
"General Hospital" fan

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:43.634
-Are you?
-from back in the day.

00:01:43.634 --> 00:01:46.133
Yeah, I'm like old-school.

00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:48.367
-Now, you got to remember,
when you say old-school,

00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:49.934
what does that mean?

00:01:49.934 --> 00:01:51.868
Because me,
I'm talking Luke and Laura.

00:01:51.868 --> 00:01:54.167
[ Oohs and applause ]
-Yeah. I'm talking about --

00:01:54.167 --> 00:01:56.234
♪ Think of Laura,
laugh, don't cry ♪

00:01:56.234 --> 00:01:58.300
♪ I know she'd
want it that way ♪
-That's right. That's right.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:01:59.133
That's right.
That's right.

00:01:59.133 --> 00:02:01.200
You talking about Felicia.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.567
That's what you talking about.
-Oh, no, no, no.

00:02:02.567 --> 00:02:04.734
Her husband --
-No, I'm talking about Bobbie.

00:02:04.734 --> 00:02:07.667
-Bobbie? Z? You talking
about Bobbie Spencer?

00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:09.300
-Bobbie Spencer, Jackie Zeman.
-That's right,

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:10.801
Jackie Zeman, Bobbie Spencer.

00:02:10.801 --> 00:02:13.367
That was Luke sister
on "General Hospital."

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:15.834
-I went to --
-You know he got --

00:02:15.834 --> 00:02:17.701
He almost died because of her.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:17.701 --> 00:02:19.567
Did you know that?
-Luke, or Tony Geary?

00:02:19.567 --> 00:02:21.534
-He was in -- Luke.

00:02:21.534 --> 00:02:24.334
He was in the elevator, okay?
-Yes.

00:02:24.334 --> 00:02:26.334
And he was trying to protect her
and got shot.

00:02:26.334 --> 00:02:27.901
Almost got shot years ago.

00:02:27.901 --> 00:02:29.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.234 --> 00:02:30.934
She almost got Luke killed.
-I know.

00:02:30.934 --> 00:02:32.200
[ Laughter ]
Bobbie's trouble, man.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.334
-You got the Cassadines,
you got the weather machine.

00:02:34.334 --> 00:02:35.667
-No, here's what happened.
The Cassadines,

00:02:35.667 --> 00:02:37.267
here's what happened.

00:02:37.267 --> 00:02:39.133
I was doing stand-up in L.A.

00:02:39.133 --> 00:02:43.334
and I got invited to lunch
at Jackie Zeman's house.

00:02:43.334 --> 00:02:44.467
-Wow!
-It was amazing.

00:02:44.467 --> 00:02:45.801
Beautiful place.

00:02:45.801 --> 00:02:49.167
And I see the
Quartermaines talking.

00:02:49.167 --> 00:02:51.133
-Well, that kind of
hurt your feelings, didn't it?

00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:52.667
-It did bum me out.
-Because, you know,
you get caught up.

00:02:52.667 --> 00:02:55.934
See, you watch a soap opera --
-Yo, this can't happen.

00:02:55.934 --> 00:02:57.467
You know, you enemies,
stay enemies!

00:02:57.467 --> 00:03:00.334
-That's exactly right!
-You can't be seen

00:03:00.334 --> 00:03:01.968
out in public like that.
-Barbecues.

00:03:01.968 --> 00:03:03.968
Exactly right! I go,
"I've got to get out."

00:03:03.968 --> 00:03:05.601
I got to get myself
out of the situation.

00:03:05.601 --> 00:03:07.033
-That's right.
-So I left.

00:03:07.033 --> 00:03:08.901
-I'm a surveillance expert
for the mob.

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:11.334
My character's name is Brick
on "General Hospital."

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:13.868
-Brick!
-Sonny Corinthos
is my boss, alright?

00:03:13.868 --> 00:03:15.167
[ Applause ]
-That's my dude.
I love Sonny Corinthos.

00:03:15.167 --> 00:03:18.367
-We so real with each other
that, even off set,

00:03:18.367 --> 00:03:20.167
if I saw you messing with him,
I might have

00:03:20.167 --> 00:03:21.734
to try and do something.
-That's what I'm talking about.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.901
[ Applause ]
-Because that's my job.
-That's exactly right.

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:26.534
-That's my job.
-Yeah. I love how
excited you get.

00:03:26.534 --> 00:03:28.601
You get me excited,
watching you.

00:03:28.601 --> 00:03:31.968
You get excited when you talk,
when you talk and then you talk

00:03:31.968 --> 00:03:33.868
about something more
and then you get excited,

00:03:33.868 --> 00:03:35.133
then you get louder!
-That's right.

00:03:35.133 --> 00:03:36.968
-You always did that?
-Not always.

00:03:36.968 --> 00:03:38.701
Well, first of all,
I'm the youngest of six

00:03:38.701 --> 00:03:40.968
and I was raised by five women.
-Yeah.

00:03:40.968 --> 00:03:42.300
-So let's be clear.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.767
I didn't talk loud too often.

00:03:43.767 --> 00:03:46.501
[ Laughter ]
Let's be very, very clear
about that.

00:03:46.501 --> 00:03:49.300
My sisters would not hesitate
to abuse me.

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:51.567
Their names are Linda,
[Indistinct],

00:03:51.567 --> 00:03:52.801
-Alright, alright, alright.
-Abigail, and Carmen.

00:03:52.801 --> 00:03:53.868
[ Laughter and applause ]
Alright?

00:03:53.868 --> 00:03:55.234
-You don't have to rat them out.

00:03:55.234 --> 00:03:57.701
-Yes, I am ratting them out
because they would beat up

00:03:57.701 --> 00:03:59.367
their little brother,
yes, they would.

00:03:59.367 --> 00:04:02.467
[ Laughter ]
But the bottom line is
it taught you --

00:04:02.467 --> 00:04:06.167
it taught me -- you talk
to ladies a certain way

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:08.567
-That's right.
-and you talk to the fellas
a certain way.

00:04:08.567 --> 00:04:10.534
-Okay.
-And so, when I get on TV,

00:04:10.534 --> 00:04:12.601
I'm projecting.
I got to make sure.

00:04:12.601 --> 00:04:14.901
If I'm not passionate
about what I'm talking about,

00:04:14.901 --> 00:04:16.901
why should you be passionate
about listening to me?

00:04:16.901 --> 00:04:18.868
So I got to do that.
But!

00:04:18.868 --> 00:04:21.400
[ Laughter ]
When the ladies are
on the air with me,

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:24.367
[ Softer ]
I have to change my tone

00:04:24.367 --> 00:04:28.000
[ Laughter ]
and modify my delivery

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.934
just a little bit, you know?

00:04:29.934 --> 00:04:31.667
That's right.
You got to, you know,

00:04:31.667 --> 00:04:33.334
[ The Roots playing
sultry funk ]
the Barry White,

00:04:33.334 --> 00:04:35.334
Teddy Pendergrass,
the Isley Brothers.

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:37.300
See, I'm from that school.
I'm from that school.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:39.701
Roots! I'm from that school!
-That's okay. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:39.701 --> 00:04:41.501
-You understand?
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:41.501 --> 00:04:45.334
-I mean, you know, these young
whippersnappers today,

00:04:45.334 --> 00:04:46.834
nah, that's not my style.
-No.

00:04:46.834 --> 00:04:49.834
-And that's how you get
"First Take," right?

00:04:49.834 --> 00:04:51.534
And then it goes
to "Stephen A's World."

00:04:51.534 --> 00:04:53.434
-Yeah. Well, "Stephen A's World"
is a little bit different.

00:04:53.434 --> 00:04:56.634
It's on ESPN+ I executive
produce that with ESPN.

00:04:56.634 --> 00:04:59.300
I could do what I want to do
there because I'm the boss.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:01.834
Now, they say I could do
what I want with "First Take,"

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.634
but the ladies run that.

00:05:03.634 --> 00:05:07.133
-I have questions
that I want to ask you.

00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:10.067
Tiger Woods in the Masters.
I thought it was pretty awesome

00:05:10.067 --> 00:05:13.267
to see that guy
and he did really well.

00:05:13.267 --> 00:05:15.567
What's your take
on Tiger Woods' comeback?

00:05:15.567 --> 00:05:17.968
-He's won already.
He can't lose.

00:05:17.968 --> 00:05:21.300
It doesn't matter what happens
this particular weekend.

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:23.834
He almost died
in a car accident.

00:05:23.834 --> 00:05:25.868
He survived
a major car accident.

00:05:25.868 --> 00:05:27.100
Then, they told him they thought

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:29.534
about amputating
a part of his leg.

00:05:29.534 --> 00:05:31.701
Then, he survived that.
Then, they said to him,

00:05:31.701 --> 00:05:33.501
"You may never walk
straight again.

00:05:33.501 --> 00:05:35.834
Don't even think about
a golf career again,"

00:05:35.834 --> 00:05:38.334
and now, he's back
at the Masters.

00:05:38.334 --> 00:05:39.534
-Yeah.
-He's already won.

00:05:39.534 --> 00:05:40.834
[ Cheering and applause ]
-That's exactly right.

00:05:40.834 --> 00:05:42.901
That's why I love.
Stephen A. Smith and I

00:05:42.901 --> 00:05:44.334
are going to play
"Wheel of Opinions"

00:05:44.334 --> 00:05:45.801
when we come back.
Stick around.

